        <argsstring>(const HypergraphType &amp;hypergraph, const std::filesystem::path &amp;path=&quot;hypergraph.hgsf&quot;, const std::initializer_list&lt; gl::io::options_manip &gt; &amp;options={})</argsstring>
        <name>save</name>
        <qualifiedname>hgl::io::save</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const HypergraphType &amp;</type>
          <declname>hypergraph</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const std::filesystem::path &amp;</type>
          <declname>path</declname>
          <defval>&quot;hypergraph.hgsf&quot;</defval>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const std::initializer_list&lt; <ref refid="classgl_1_1io_1_1options__manip" kindref="compound">gl::io::options_manip</ref> &gt; &amp;</type>
          <declname>options</declname>
          <defval>{}</defval>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Serializes and saves a hypergraph to a file. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Writes the topology and optionally the properties of the hypergraph to the specified file using the Hypergraph Specification Format (HGSF). By default, The function strictly respects the <ref refid="group__HGL-IO_1ga122e8e1c01d620ad256cbc6fa4b11c7a" kindref="member">write</ref> and <ref refid="group__HGL-IO_1ga68c7a56059c564fcab9ffd8d46213773" kindref="member">append</ref> safety guards.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>HypergraphType</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The concrete type of the hypergraph being saved. Must satisfy <ulink url="hgl_concepts.md#hgl-traits-c-hypergraph"><bold>c_hypergraph</bold></ulink>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Mode</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The file access mode (e.g., <ref refid="group__HGL-IO_1ga122e8e1c01d620ad256cbc6fa4b11c7a" kindref="member">write</ref> or <ref refid="group__HGL-IO_1ga68c7a56059c564fcab9ffd8d46213773" kindref="member">append</ref>). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>hypergraph</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The hypergraph instance to serialize. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>path</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The filesystem path where the hypergraph will be saved. Defaults to <computeroutput>&quot;hypergraph.hgsf&quot;</computeroutput>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>options</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>An optional initializer list of stream manipulators to configure the output (e.g., <computeroutput>{<ref refid="group__HGL-IO_1ga8735be586da90ff9701dd5a4a7bc5398" kindref="member">hgl::io::with_properties</ref>}</computeroutput>). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="exception"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>std::filesystem::filesystem_error</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>If file safety checks fail (e.g., overwriting an existing file in <computeroutput>write</computeroutput> mode). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>std::ios_base::failure</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>If the underlying file stream cannot be opened. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
